From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sechost, services: SubscribeServiceChangeNotifications; a manager handle reports services created and deleted

SubscribeServiceChangeNotifications and UnsubscribeServiceChangeNotifications
were stubs: a program calling one ended ("unimplemented function"). WireGuard
for Windows' manager service watches the service database with it
(SC_EVENT_DATABASE_CHANGE on the service control manager's handle) and each
tunnel service's status (SC_EVENT_STATUS_CHANGE); it ended at once, and its
installer hung (i0977). They are now implemented as on Windows: the callback
is called on a thread of the subscription's own with the SERVICE_NOTIFY_* bit
of what happened -- the service's new state, or a service created or deleted
-- and never again once Unsubscribe has returned (it waits for a callback that
is running). Each change is a NotifyServiceStatusChange registration made again
after it fires, on a handle the subscription opens for itself where it can, so
that the caller's handle stays free for its own NotifyServiceStatusChange or
another subscription, and Unsubscribe ends the wait by closing it.

services.exe answered NotifyServiceStatusChange on a manager handle with
ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED. A manager handle now reports services created and
deleted (SERVICE_NOTIFY_CREATED, SERVICE_NOTIFY_DELETED) with their names in
pszServiceNames ("/name" created, "\name" deleted, a multi-string the caller
frees with LocalFree, as Windows documents it); what changes between two
registrations is kept for the next one. Programs still on the Windows 7 way of
watching for new services (WireGuard's fallback among them) work too.

Test: test/svcsubscribe-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit): a manager subscription is
told of a service created and deleted, and of nothing before; a service
subscription of its start and stop; after Unsubscribe the callback is not
called again, and a second subscription on the same handle works. Mutants
SG_MUTANT_NO_DATABASE_NOTIFY (programs/services/rpc.c), SG_MUTANT_SUBSCRIBE_STUB
and SG_MUTANT_SUBSCRIBE_SHARED_HANDLE (dlls/sechost/service.c) each fail it.
